{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116320",
      "title": "Showing a Loading Fallback",
      "lectureOrder": 227,
      "videoOrder": 216,
      "sourceHash": "2d87bee13c6d18c8e1742e158ee648ca3b12fa80c0cb0a2e97a83e150df6428f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.57,
          "end": 2.85,
          "en": "So we got this delay",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.85,
          "end": 5.31,
          "en": "when we were fetching our places data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.31,
          "end": 8.16,
          "en": "and it would be nice to show some fallback,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.16,
          "end": 9.21,
          "en": "some fallback text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.21,
          "end": 11.31,
          "en": "or some loading spinner to the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.31,
          "end": 13.953,
          "en": "whilst we're waiting for the places to arrive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.82,
          "end": 18.9,
          "en": "And it turns out that this is fairly straightforward",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.9,
          "end": 21.48,
          "en": "and simple to implement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.48,
          "end": 24.57,
          "en": "because one nice option we have here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.57,
          "end": 27.78,
          "en": "one easy way of adding this feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.78,
          "end": 30.69,
          "en": "is that we add another Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.69,
          "end": 32.67,
          "en": "for example called isFetching,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.67,
          "end": 33.97,
          "en": "but the name is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.89,
          "end": 38.223,
          "en": "and set it to false initially, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.08,
          "end": 44.64,
          "en": "and then an ngOnInit when we're about to send this request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.64,
          "end": 47.52,
          "en": "So when we're about to start fetching data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.52,
          "end": 51.753,
          "en": "we simply update isFetching and set it to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.15,
          "end": 56.04,
          "en": "And then we just wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.04,
          "end": 59.343,
          "en": "that we set it back to false once we're done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.51,
          "end": 64.5,
          "en": "For that, we can also register a complete function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.5,
          "end": 65.733,
          "en": "in our observer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.57,
          "end": 68.67,
          "en": "because that complete function will run",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.67,
          "end": 72.12,
          "en": "once this entire process is done,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.12,
          "end": 75.66,
          "en": "which is also the case, of course, in the next function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.66,
          "end": 79.2,
          "en": "since only one value will be emitted here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.2,
          "end": 82.71000000000001,
          "en": "But in case we would configure this request differently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.71000000000001,
          "end": 87.09,
          "en": "to emit multiple values or anything like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.09,
          "end": 90.09,
          "en": "we are safer if we use complete",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.09,
          "end": 92.97,
          "en": "because that's guaranteed to only run once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.97,
          "end": 97.97,
          "en": "once the observable and the offered request is done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.16,
          "end": 99.78,
          "en": "So it's in this complete function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.78,
          "end": 103.22999999999999,
          "en": "where I now want to set isFetching back to false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.22999999999999,
          "end": 106.143,
          "en": "by calling the set method on the Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.96000000000001,
          "end": 112.8,
          "en": "And now all we have to do is go to our template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.8,
          "end": 115.863,
          "en": "the available-places.component template file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.06,
          "end": 120.54,
          "en": "and in there, I'm only rendering my app-places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.54,
          "end": 125.54,
          "en": "if I have places, which is not the case initially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.76,
          "end": 129.393,
          "en": "because we start with undefined as an initial value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.83,
          "end": 133.53,
          "en": "but we can now in addition also render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.53,
          "end": 136.98,
          "en": "some other conditional content with @if",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 136.98,
          "end": 139.2,
          "en": "or with the ngif directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 139.2,
          "end": 142.203,
          "en": "if you are using an older version of Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.22,
          "end": 148.22,
          "en": "But with @if, we can check if isFetching is truthy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.62,
          "end": 150.32999999999998,
          "en": "and if that's the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 150.32999999999998,
          "end": 152.73,
          "en": "then I want to output a paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 152.73,
          "end": 157.07999999999998,
          "en": "with a class of fallback-text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.07999999999998,
          "end": 162.07999999999998,
          "en": "where we could say Fetching available places...",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 164.25,
          "end": 166.923,
          "en": "And you can of course output whatever you want here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 167.88,
          "end": 169.35,
          "en": "And this should now be shown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 169.35,
          "end": 172.803,
          "en": "as long as we're waiting for the places data to arrive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 174.42000000000002,
          "end": 176.04,
          "en": "So if we save that and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 176.04,
          "end": 177.78,
          "en": "we see that text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.78,
          "end": 180,
          "en": "but then after a while, the places are there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 180,
          "end": 181.683,
          "en": "and we see those instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.82,
          "end": 185.1,
          "en": "And that's one quick and easy way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 185.1,
          "end": 189.453,
          "en": "of showing such a isFetching fallback state.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
